From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Don't make supplementary service requests
 blocking

0fe249d gave supplementary service requests a 5 minute timeout and made
them blocking. A blocking request stops its client until it completes,
and call settings and call forwarding share voice_client with call
control, call barring sim_client with SIM I/O.

The RIL of the Mindphone (MT6739) runs one supplementary service
request at a time for both SIMs and queues the rest; in one log 8 of
them took more than 30 seconds, the slowest 52.8. While the settings
page reads them, hanging up or answering a call would wait for that.
Keep the long timeout, drop the blocking.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/binder_call_barring.c    | 9 ++++-----
 src/binder_call_forwarding.c | 9 ++++-----
 src/binder_call_settings.c   | 9 ++++-----
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/binder_call_barring.c b/src/binder_call_barring.c
index 20ae633..3406941 100644
--- a/src/binder_call_barring.c
+++ b/src/binder_call_barring.c
@@ -158,13 +158,12 @@ binder_call_barring_req_new(
         binder_call_barring_callback_data_new(self, cb, data));
 
     /*
-     * Supplementary service requests may take a long time. Make them
-     * blocking to avoid disturbing the modem while it's talking to the
-     * carrier. These requests are typically initiated by the user from
-     * the system settings.
+     * Supplementary service requests may take a long time. They are not
+     * made blocking: a blocking request holds up everything else on the
+     * client, and call settings and call forwarding share voice_client
+     * with call control, call barring sim_client with SIM I/O.
      */
     radio_request_set_timeout(req, BINDER_SS_TIMEOUT_MS);
-    radio_request_set_blocking(req, TRUE);
     return req;
 }
 
